{"chunk_id": "6400c53252ff", "text": "Lomasa narrates to Yudhishthira the origins of the legend that will eventually lead to the descent of the Ganga. King Sagara of the Ikshvaku line performs severe austerities to obtain children. Siva grants a strange boon: one wife will bear a single heir who will continue the lineage, while the other will produce sixty thousand sons who will ultimately perish together. The sons grow powerful but arrogant and violent. During Sagara\u2019s horse sacrifice, the sacred horse disappears, and the princes dig through the earth and the ocean in their search, causing immense destruction. They eventually find the horse near the sage Kapila but rashly attack him and are burned to ashes by his fiery glance. Sagara\u2019s grandson Ansuman respectfully approaches Kapila, retrieves the horse, and learns that a future descendant\u2014Bhagiratha\u2014will bring the Ganga to earth to purify the dead princes. The episode explains the moral contrast between arrogance and humility and sets up the famous Ganga myth.\nKing Sagara\u2019s 60,000 sons dig the earth seeking a stolen sacrificial horse, anger sage Kapila, are burned to ashes, and prophecy foretells Ganga\u2019s future descent.\nThemes: divine prophecy, arrogance and punishment, royal duty, ascetic power, origins of Ganga legend", "vector": [0.015501155517995358, -0.01768309623003006, -0.00038380586192943156, 0.009477389976382256, -0.0111640440300107, 0.01862012781202793, -0.03954267129302025, 0.013894817791879177, -0.026410862803459167, -0.024202149361371994, 0.008031686767935753, 0.011297905817627907, 0.012797154486179352, 0.010200242511928082, 0.0024161990731954575, 0.010990024544298649, 0.042728573083877563, -0.026986466720700264, 0.027548685669898987, -0.002384406980127096, 0.0027073477394878864, -0.009504162706434727, 0.005260754842311144, 0.02942274510860443, -0.02797704190015793, 0.02608959563076496, 0.022127296775579453, -0.010983331128954887, -0.00640527019277215, -0.01014000456780